@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+---
+name: changelog
+description: Adds the entry for a change to CHANGELOG.md, one line under [Unreleased] in its Keep a Changelog section. Use when someone asks to add a change to the changelog or to update CHANGELOG.md for their work. Not for release notes to users, and not for releasing a version.
+---
+
+# Changelog entry
+
+Our apps keep `CHANGELOG.md` in the Keep a Changelog format. Each pull request adds its entry under
+`## [Unreleased]`; the version-bump skill moves those entries under the version when it is released.
+
+1. Find out what the change does for the people who read the changelog: from the person, or from the branch
+   (the diff and the log against `main`).
+2. Choose its section: `Added` for something new, `Changed` for a change to what exists, `Deprecated` for
+   something that will go, `Removed` for something gone, `Fixed` for a bug fix, `Security` for a vulnerability.
+3. Under `## [Unreleased]`, add the section heading (`### Fixed`) if it is not there, in the order above, and the
+   entry below it: one line, starting with `- `, in plain words, saying what changed for the reader. No date, no
+   version, no hash.
+
+   ```
+   ## [Unreleased]
+
+   ### Added
+   - Reports can be exported as CSV from their menu.
+
+   ### Fixed
+   - Signing in no longer loops back to the login page after a password change.
+   ```
+
+4. Never add a version heading or a date: a release does that.
